<title>UK: Freighter runs aground in strong winds at Veracruz.</title>
<headline>Freighter runs aground in strong winds at Veracruz.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cyprus-flagged freighter Nika II ran aground in gale force nine winds at Veracruz anchorage, Mexico, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 15,251 dwt vessel was awaiting berthing instructions when strong winds caused it to drift and run aground.</p>
<p>A diver inspection will be carried out on February 18.</p>
<p>The Nika II sailed from Abidjan on January 23 and was inbound to Veracruz to load a cargo of bagged sugar for Algeria.</p>
</text>
